  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI just installed matrix-synapse and tried a few things. First thing I noticed is, that it doesn't bind to IPv6 adresses (well, yes, known bug). The other is, that it actually tries to use IPv6 adresses:\r\n2017-03-28 00:19:39,361 - synapse.http.matrixfederationclient - 183 - WARNING - POST-158- {GET-O-1} Sending request failed to matrix.org: GET matrix://matrix.org/_matrix/federation/v1/publicRooms?include_all_networks=true&limit=20: InvalidAddressError - InvalidAddressError: IPv4 port write() called with IPv6 address\r\n2017-03-28 00:19:39,361 - synapse.http.outbound - 209 - INFO - POST-158- {GET-O-1} [matrix.org] Result: InvalidAddressError - InvalidAddressError: IPv4 port write() called with IPv6 address\r\n",
